  "system": {
    "description": {
      "type": "String",
      "label": "Description",
      "value": "<p>The bullet hits high on your hip, smashing in right between the lesser and greater trochanter protuberances near the head of the thigh bone, transforming it into a mess of splintered bone fragments. A complicated fracture like that will never heal and the dead bone fragments will inevitably lead to infection and gangrene. The whole leg will have to come out!</p><p><strong>Effects:</strong> Gain @Condition[Prone] and @Condition[Stunned] (3). The leg is useless – @UUID[Compendium.wfrp4e-core.items.Item.k00PimCWkff11IA0]{Amputation (Hard)}. After the encounter you’ll need <strong>Surgery (Difficult)</strong> within a week as the leg will have to be amputated at the hip or you’ll contract @UUID[Compendium.wfrp4e-core.items.Item.M8XyRs9DN12XsFTQ]{Blood Rot} as the extremity turns gangrenous. </p><p>No Extraction is necessary, as any remaining bullet fragments not removed with the leg or coming out with the flood of pus won’t really make much of a difference to your health.</p>"
    },
